{
  "$comment": "Conformance fixture for the coarse redaction kill switches (Phase 6 W7). Every implementation (TS @graphmind-ai/client, Python graphmind, Ruby graphmind) must turn each case's `in` events into exactly its `out` events when the given switches are on. Events are `{type, payload}` in emit order within ONE run; a fresh redactor per case (kind tracking starts empty). Switch names are the option names; the env names are GRAPHMIND_HIDE_INPUTS / _OUTPUTS / _TOOL_ARGS / _TOOL_RESULTS (on for any value except empty, 0, false, off and no, case-insensitive — a privacy switch fails closed on spelling). Rules: node.started.input -> placeholder under hideInputs, or under hideToolArgs when kind is tool; node.finished.output -> placeholder under hideOutputs, or under hideToolResults when the instance's kind is tool (kind comes from the matching node.started; without an instanceId the node's latest kind; unknown node -> a `tool:` nodeId prefix); node.token deltas keep `t` and gain `chars` (the text length) with `v` emptied — all deltas under hideOutputs, deltas of tool nodes under hideToolResults, `tool-args` deltas under hideToolArgs and hideInputs; node.error is never redacted; a field that is absent, or already the placeholder, is left alone and not counted; `redaction.count` is the number of values replaced and `redaction.keys` the payload fields touched; an existing `redaction` on the payload is merged (counts add, keys union). Names, kinds, ids, timings, usage and every other field survive untouched. Fail closed (decisions.md \"Redaction fails closed on internal error\"): with any switch on, a node.started/node.finished/node.token event the redactor cannot inspect (the payload is not an object, a property read throws, token `deltas` that is not an array while a hiding switch could cover it, a covered delta that is neither null nor an object, a covered delta whose `v` is present and not a string) is replaced by its failed form, built WITHOUT reading input/output/deltas: node.started {nodeId, parentId?, kind, name, instanceId, input: placeholder}, node.finished {nodeId, instanceId?, durationMs, heldMs?, status, usage?, output: placeholder}, node.token {nodeId, instanceId?, deltas: []}, each with redaction {count: 0, keys: [\"input\",\"output\",\"deltas\"], failed: true}; every other field is omitted; an optional field whose read throws or whose value is not schema-valid is omitted; when a required field cannot be read or is not schema-valid (nodeId/name/instanceId strings, kind a NodeKind, durationMs a finite number >= 0, status ok|error|aborted) the event is dropped, shown in `out` as {type, dropped: true}. `chars` is the UTF-16 code unit count (JS string length: an astral character counts 2). Tool calls (0.6.0+): under hideToolArgs or hideInputs (the switches that hide `tool-args` deltas), and when the output is not already hidden whole, the arguments of each entry of an object output's own `toolCalls` array — the fields `input`, `inputText`, and the older spellings `arguments` and `args`, wherever present and not undefined or already the placeholder — become the placeholder, counted one per value under the key \"output.toolCalls\"; a `toolCalls` that is not an array, or an entry that is neither null nor an object, is replaced whole (counted 1); names, ids and every other field survive; this applies to every node kind. hideOutputs (and hideToolResults on a tool instance) replace the whole output first, so its toolCalls are never counted separately. Usage in the failed form (0.6.0+): `usage` keeps inputTokens and outputTokens (both required, non-negative safe integers, else no usage), `inclusive` when it is a boolean, and cacheReadTokens / cacheWriteTokens / reasoningTokens when each is a non-negative safe integer; every other usage field is dropped. Pause answers (0.6.0+, contract C2): an exec.resumed / exec.refused event in `in` may carry `nodeKind`, the paused node's kind as the session passes it to the redactor (absent: unknown, which counts as a tool); `out` entries never carry it. A pause answer is covered exactly when the paused node's input is — hideInputs, or hideToolArgs when the kind is tool or unknown: exec.resumed.edited becomes {after: placeholder} (left alone and not counted when it is already exactly that; absent: nothing to hide), counted under the key \"edited\", and exec.refused.message is omitted (present, even null: counted under \"message\"); every other field survives and an existing summary is merged. Not covered (another switch, or another kind under hideToolArgs): the payload is returned as it is, whatever it holds. Covered but not inspectable (the payload is not an object, or `pauseId` is present, not null and not a string): the failed form — {pauseId, action, edited?: {after: placeholder}, requestId?} or {pauseId, code, requestId?}, with redaction {count: 0, keys: [\"edited\"] or [\"message\"], failed: true} — needs a string pauseId and a valid action / code, so from JSON alone such an event is dropped; the failed form itself (a payload whose fields cannot be read) is pinned by each port's unit tests.",
  "placeholder": "__REDACTED__",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "hideInputs replaces node.started.input on every kind, nothing else",
      "switches": { "hideInputs": true },
      "in": [
        { "type": "run.started", "payload": { "app": "a", "sdk": { "name": "t", "version": "1" } } },
        { "type": "node.started", "payload": { "nodeId": "agent:run", "kind": "agent", "name": "run", "instanceId": "r1", "input": { "prompt": "SECRET-PROMPT" } } },
        { "type": "node.started", "payload": { "nodeId": "llm:step", "kind": "llm", "name": "step", "instanceId": "l1", "parentId": "agent:run", "input": { "messages": ["SECRET-PROMPT"] } } },
        { "type": "node.started", "payload": { "nodeId": "tool:search", "kind": "tool", "name": "search", "instanceId": "t1", "input": { "q": "SECRET-ARG" } } },
        { "type": "node.finished", "payload": { "nodeId": "tool:search", "instanceId": "t1", "output": { "hits": 3 }, "durationMs": 12, "status": "ok" } },
        { "type": "node.finished", "payload": { "nodeId": "llm:step", "instanceId": "l1", "output": { "text": "SECRET-OUTPUT" }, "usage": { "inputTokens": 10, "outputTokens": 5 }, "durationMs": 800, "status": "ok" } },
        { "type": "node.finished", "payload": { "nodeId": "agent:run", "instanceId": "r1", "output": "done", "durationMs": 900, "status": "ok" } },
        { "type": "run.finished", "payload": { "status": "ok" } }
      ],
      "out": [
        { "type": "run.started", "payload": { "app": "a", "sdk": { "name": "t", "version": "1" } } },
        { "type": "node.started", "payload": { "nodeId": "agent:run", "kind": "agent", "name": "run", "instanceId": "r1", "input": "__REDACTED__", "redaction": { "count": 1, "keys": ["input"] } } },
        { "type": "node.started", "payload": { "nodeId": "llm:step", "kind": "llm", "name": "step", "instanceId": "l1", "parentId": "agent:run", "input": "__REDACTED__", "redaction": { "count": 1, "keys": ["input"] } } },
        { "type": "node.started", "payload": { "nodeId": "tool:search", "kind": "tool", "name": "search", "instanceId": "t1", "input": "__REDACTED__", "redaction": { "count": 1, "keys": ["input"] } } },
        { "type": "node.finished", "payload": { "nodeId": "tool:search", "instanceId": "t1", "output": { "hits": 3 }, "durationMs": 12, "status": "ok" } },
        { "type": "node.finished", "payload": { "nodeId": "llm:step", "instanceId": "l1", "output": { "text": "SECRET-OUTPUT" }, "usage": { "inputTokens": 10, "outputTokens": 5 }, "durationMs": 800, "status": "ok" } },
        { "type": "node.finished", "payload": { "nodeId": "agent:run", "instanceId": "r1", "output": "done", "durationMs": 900, "status": "ok" } },
        { "type": "run.finished", "payload": { "status": "ok" } }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "hideOutputs replaces node.finished.output on every kind and empties token deltas, keeping counts",
      "switches": { "hideOutputs": true },
      "in": [
        { "type": "node.started", "payload": { "nodeId": "llm:step", "kind": "llm", "name": "step", "instanceId": "l1", "input": { "messages": ["hi"] } } },
        { "type": "node.token", "payload": { "nodeId": "llm:step", "deltas": [{ "t": "text", "v": "Hello" }, { "t": "reasoning", "v": "thinking…" }, { "t": "tool-args", "v": "{\"q\":1}" }] } },
        { "type": "node.token", "payload": { "nodeId": "llm:step", "deltas": [{ "t": "text", "v": "" }] } },
        { "type": "node.finished", "payload": { "nodeId": "llm:step", "instanceId": "l1", "output": { "text": "Hello" }, "usage": { "inputTokens": 3, "outputTokens": 2 }, "durationMs": 40, "status": "ok" } },
        { "type": "node.started", "payload": { "nodeId": "tool:search", "kind": "tool", "name": "search", "instanceId": "t1", "input": { "q": 1 } } },
        { "type": "node.finished", "payload": { "nodeId": "tool:search", "instanceId": "t1", "output": [1, 2, 3], "durationMs": 5, "status": "ok" } }
      ],
      "out": [
        { "type": "node.started", "payload": { "nodeId": "llm:step", "kind": "llm", "name": "step", "instanceId": "l1", "input": { "messages": ["hi"] } } },
        { "type": "node.token", "payload": { "nodeId": "llm:step", "deltas": [{ "t": "text", "v": "", "chars": 5 }, { "t": "reasoning", "v": "", "chars": 9 }, { "t": "tool-args", "v": "", "chars": 7 }], "redaction": { "count": 3, "keys": ["deltas"] } } },
        { "type": "node.token", "payload": { "nodeId": "llm:step", "deltas": [{ "t": "text", "v": "" }] } },
        { "type": "node.finished", "payload": { "nodeId": "llm:step", "instanceId": "l1", "output": "__REDACTED__", "usage": { "inputTokens": 3, "outputTokens": 2 }, "durationMs": 40, "status": "ok", "redaction": { "count": 1, "keys": ["output"] } } },
        { "type": "node.started", "payload": { "nodeId": "tool:search", "kind": "tool", "name": "search", "instanceId": "t1", "input": { "q": 1 } } },
        { "type": "node.finished", "payload": { "nodeId": "tool:search", "instanceId": "t1", "output": "__REDACTED__", "durationMs": 5, "status": "ok", "redaction": { "count": 1, "keys": ["output"] } } }
      ]
